===Etymology===
From {{bor|en|fr|Québec}}, from {{der|en|alq|kepék|gloss=(it) narrows}}. Cognate with {{cog|mic|gepe'g|t=plug}}, and {{cog|mic|Kepinkek}}<sup>[https://www.google.com/maps/place/Kepenkeck+Lake/@48.2973521,-54.9466376,8z/data=!4m6!3m5!1s0x4b7159c5440a6577:0xd4c71d5c80b00f03!8m2!3d48.2973545!4d-54.926038!16s%2Fg%2F11clghs9gl?entry=ttu&g_ep=EgoyMDI0MTEwNi4wIKXMDSoASAFQAw%3D%3D]</sup>; compare Proto-Algonquian {{l|alg-pro|''*kepahikani''||obstruction}}. It originally referred to the area around {{w|lang=en|Quebec City}} where the {{w|lang=en|Saint Lawrence River}} narrows to a cliff-lined gap. The name of the city preceded that of the province.

